<section class="orders-section">
	<h2>Knightly Orders of Crusaders</h2>
	<p>Without a meaningful cause to pursue, a knight would be little more than a well-versed brawler. What exactly this
		driving force is varies from knight to knight, but chief among these motives is faith. Whether pursuing Torag's
		favor by showing unwavering courage in the face of battle or spreading the word of Sarenrae's wisdom with a flaming
		sword, knight dedicated to holy and unholy orders are as multitudinous as they are varied. Since knights join the
		crusades for a myriad of reasons, they do not all take the same form, but generally fall into the following broad
		types: Heavy Knights wearing sturdy armor and wielding great weapons, Thaumaturgic Knights wielding arcane or divine
		magic as their primary means of gallantry, and Unhindered Knights who favor lightweight garb and perform their
		duties with unparalleled grace.</p>
	<ul class="toggleLiVis" style="list-style-type: none;">
		<li style="display: none;"><b>Click to Unfold the Knightly Orders' Forward:</b></li>
		<li><b>Click to Fold-up the Knightly Orders' Forward:</b></li>
		<li>It can be incredibly useful to recognize and distinguish the various knightly orders, both holy and unholy, that
			are involved in the crusades, as knight devoted to the same order typically also share principles and goals, as
			well as common patron deities and recruitment practices. Being able to locate and identify a riftwarden, eagle
			knight, or cultist by their signs, tokens, and symbols, can save your life in a crisis and the shared culture can
			go a long way for cutting through lengthy introductions. Membership in these orders is also a privilege that needs
			to be earned, and many adventurers may dedicate the next step of their lived to pursuing admission to their ranks.
			The predominant knightly orders present amongst crusaders include the following:</li>
	</ul>
	<br>
	<% if (!orders || orders.length === 0) { %>
	<p>No orders have been discovered yet.</p>
	<% } else { %>
	<div class="asset">

		<% orders.forEach(t => { %>

		<section class="<%= t.attitude_id === 5 ? 'hostile'
                        : t.attitude_id === 4 ? 'unfriendly'
                        : t.attitude_id === 3 ? 'neutral'
                        : t.attitude_id === 2 ? 'friendly'
                        : 'helpful' %>">

			<h3><%= t.faction_name %></h3>
			<!-- <strong>Leader: None</strong><br><br> -->

			<figure class="<%= t.is_tall ? 'two-three' : 'one-one' %>">
				<picture>
					<% if (t.image_url) { %>
					<source srcset="<%= t.image_url %>" type="image/webp">
					<img src="<%= t.image_url %>" alt="<%= t.alt || t.faction_name %>">
					<% } else { %>
					<img src="/images/core/unknown.png" alt="<%= t.faction_name %>">
					<% } %>
				</picture>
			</figure>

			<% if (t.description) { %>
			<p><%= t.description %></p>
			<% } %>

			<% if (t.extra_list.length > 0) { %>
			<ul style="list-style-type: lower-greek;">
				<% t.extra_list.forEach(item => { %>
				<li><%= item %></li>
				<% }) %>
			</ul>
			<% } %>

		</section>

		<% }) %>

	</div>
	<% } %>
</section>